  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "07d7c37b-4345-4721-9f70-4a8c8b935d53",
      "name": "Physical Experimentation",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Floors have thresholds. Rooms have awkward corners. Wireless connections fail. Batteries run down. People walk through the path you carefully planned.\n\nReal environments have an efficient way of exposing assumptions.\n\nThat is why Myomaton is built around physical experimentation rather than demonstrations that work only under ideal conditions.",
        "heading": "Reality is an excellent design review"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 60,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "wide",
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "normal",
        "alignment": "left",
        "treatment": "statement",
        "composition": "statement-break"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1d8815d4-147a-4f27-8e2b-65ca703e024e",
      "name": "Principles",
      "type": "collection",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "principle-001",
            "text": "Practical robotics becomes much more interesting when ordinary hardware can participate.",
            "heading": "Affordable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-002",
            "text": "The system should be possible to inspect, explain, modify, and repair.",
            "heading": "Understandable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-003",
            "text": "Useful machines should not become disposable because one component or service disappears.",
            "heading": "Repairable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-004",
            "text": "Core behavior and safety should remain close to the robot rather than depending unnecessarily on remote services.",
            "heading": "Local-first"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-005",
            "text": "Cloud and AI services can add capability, but basic ownership and usefulness should not depend on continuing payments or Internet access.",
            "heading": "No mandatory cloud or subscription"
          }
        ],
        "heading": "What makes something Myomaton?",
        "itemSource": "inline"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "grid",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 70,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "standard",
        "columns": 2,
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "compact",
        "surface": "default",
        "alignment": "left",
        "composition": "grouped-field"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1fb0bdd2-c451-4ca9-ab05-9c525685a768",
      "name": "More Than One Robot",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "A useful robot may not need to do everything.\n\nA household can make more sense as a small ecosystem: different robots with different capabilities, sharing information and helping one another where useful.",
        "heading": "More Than One Robot"
      },
      "page_id": "c4bcb2b1-84e0-4ef5-a374-383563ed7c85",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "sort_order": 60,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "wide",
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "normal",
        "surface": "default",
        "alignment": "left",
        "composition": "editorial-row"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "211ff9f7-07fc-43df-9780-1f0ea771c047",
      "name": "TaBot",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "TaBot is a practical rolling robot exploring useful household behavior — following, approaching when called, navigating real spaces, managing its own power, and eventually working alongside other robots.\n\nIt is where many Myomaton ideas meet physical reality: navigation, sensing, charging, safety, mechanical design, and the question of what behavior is actually useful around people.",
        "heading": "TaBot"
      },
      "page_id": "c4bcb2b1-84e0-4ef5-a374-383563ed7c85",
      "variant": "split-text-first",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "sort_order": 20,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "wide",
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "normal",
        "surface": "default",
        "mediaFit": "natural",
