    {
      "id": "49547304-277d-4a19-aa56-2bc19380feb4",
      "name": "Complexity has a cost",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Sophistication is useful when it earns its keep.\n\nMyomaton favors systems that can be understood, repaired, and reasoned about. More complexity should be added when it produces clear practical value, not simply because it is technically possible.",
        "heading": "Complexity has a cost"
      },
      "page_id": "5cdc56f1-d2f4-4d66-a0f8-d3871a612176",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "sort_order": 40,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "reading",
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "compact",
        "surface": "default",
        "alignment": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4fd4e176-26a4-4c5a-b3dd-d626d80b3c29",
      "name": "Small robot experiments",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Not every experiment needs to become a permanent project.\n\nSmaller platforms such as Q-Scout, Root, and other inexpensive robots let us test specific ideas quickly — charging, communication, shared control, sensing, and the division of work between simple and more capable machines.\n\nWhen an experiment develops durable identity and value, it can become a first-class Project Subject later.",
        "heading": "Small robot experiments"
      },
      "page_id": "c4bcb2b1-84e0-4ef5-a374-383563ed7c85",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "sort_order": 50,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "width": "reading",
        "divider": "none",
        "spacing": "compact",
        "surface": "default",
        "alignment": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "541bed47-e1e4-43d0-8229-b78c8ec91d8f",
      "name": "Projects",
      "type": "hero",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Working robots, experiments, and systems built to answer practical questions.",
        "heading": "Projects"
      },
      "page_id": "c4bcb2b1-84e0-4ef5-a374-383563ed7c85",
      "variant": "default",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "sort_order": 10,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-03T13:56:01.392948+00:00",
      "configuration": {
